map-board max-width 468, width 100%, aspect-ratio 5/8, so height 748.8. map heading etc. To fit viewport 763 with runbar 66 and padding 22, height available ~630; board should max-height ~560. We can set `max-height: calc(100dvh - 200px)` and width auto? CSS aspect-ratio with max-height and width 100% doesn't shrink width automatically unless width:auto and height. E.g.:
```
.map-board { width: min(100%, 468px); max-height: calc(100dvh - 210px); aspect-ratio: 5/8; }
```
max-height overrides height computed? With aspect-ratio and width set, max-height constrains height, but element width may remain 468 causing distorted? Actually max-height with aspect-ratio should reduce used height but width remains -> aspect ratio breaks? CSS aspect-ratio is a preferred ratio; max-height clamps height but width remains as specified, so ratio breaks. Better use `height: min(748px, calc(100dvh - 230px)); width: auto; aspect-ratio: 5/8; max-width: 100%;` But width auto with aspect ratio and explicit height computes width. Need also `min-height`. Let's define:
```
.map-board {
  height: min(72dvh, 748px);
  width: auto;
  max-width: 100%;
  aspect-ratio: 5 / 8;
}
```
At viewport 763, 72dvh = 549; width 343. That's small but fits. Could use 68dvh. Node sizes fixed 34px might overlap at 343x549 (tile 68px), nodes 34, okay. Boss 50. Fine. Labels 6px. At larger screens 72dvh maybe 700, width 437, close to 468. Good. In grid, map-board width auto. On mobile, use height maybe 62dvh and max-width. Let's check media rules for map-board currently.

